# bat reads ~/.config/bat/config on macOS as well as Linux, so unlike Nushell and lazygit it needs no platform-path symlink.
#
# `ansi` resolves every syntax colour through the terminal's sixteen ANSI slots,
# which this repo renders from [palette] into the Ghostty config.
# That makes the palette the single owner of what a man page or a `bat`-ed file looks like.
# The alternative — vendoring a Tokyo Night .tmTheme and running `bat cache --build` — gives finer-grained syntax colours in exchange for an asset to keep current and a cache that can go stale without saying so.
--theme=ansi

# man pages arrive already wrapped; re-wrapping them mangles tables.
--style=plain
--paging=auto
